Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Mirror NOTARGETWIN32 guard around the second winstackpagesize site (fpc 0.99)
License: expat

Same fix as fpc-1.0.6-cga-notargetwin32-guard.patch, applied to the
fpc-0.99.14 source tree (where the file is named `cgai386.pas'
rather than i386/cga.pas; the i386 backend isn't split into its own
subdir yet in 0.99).

cgai386.pas brings `t_win32' into its uses clause only via
`{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}', and `winstackpagesize' is declared in
t_win32.  The first use site (line ~2820) is correctly wrapped in
`{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}'; the second (the stack-frame setup at
line ~3186) is not -- it just runtime-guards on
`target_os.id=os_i386_win32'.  Compiling with `-dNOTARGETWIN32'
therefore drops `t_win32' from the uses clause and the unguarded
site fails to resolve `winstackpagesize' at parse time.

Wrap the second site's win32 arm (condition + body) in the same
`{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}' block; the
`else exprasmlist^.insert(... SUB stackframe ...)' fallback is left
unconditional and becomes the only branch when win32 is
unsupported.

--- a/compiler/cgai386.pas
+++ b/compiler/cgai386.pas
@@ -3183,6 +3183,7 @@
                       else
 {$endif unused}
                           begin
+{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}
                             { windows guards only a few pages for stack growing, }
                             { so we have to access every page first              }
                             if (target_os.id=os_i386_win32) and
@@ -3224,6 +3225,7 @@
                                     end
                               end
                             else
+{$endif NOTARGETWIN32}
                               exprasmlist^.insert(new(paicpu,op_const_reg(A_SUB,S_L,stackframe,R_ESP)));
                             if (cs_check_stack in aktlocalswitches) and
                               not(target_info.target in [target_i386_linux,target_i386_win32]) then
